1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:38,880
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,240
Luke!

4
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,160
Look. Just look at what you've done.

5
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:03,800
Have you lost your mind?

6
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,840
Don't move.

7
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,680
I'm gonna smack you.

8
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:11,960
Take that.

9
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,200
Let's see if you dare do it again.

10
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,680
Next time you trash the place,

11
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,080
I'll throw you out and let you be a stray.

12
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,640
Playing pitiful now?

13
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,360
Just like your mom.

14
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:30,840
Come here!

15
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,560
Don't give me that.

16
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:56,800
All right.

17
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,000
Have a treat.

18
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,520
Paw.

19
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:14,760
And this one.

20
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:18,520
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED
DURING THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

21
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,720
What happened to your paw?

22
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:24,480
Does it hurt?

23
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,200
Does it hurt, Luke?

24
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:31,720
It's okay.

25
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,040
Hello?

26
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,680
Has your dog's paw ever lost fur?

27
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,520
Will it kill him?

28
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:41,680
<i>Oh no. It's terminal.</i>

29
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:46,080
What should I do?

30
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,080
Which hospital should I take him to?

31
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:50,760
<i>I'm messing with you. Relax.</i>

32
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,520
<i>Ms. Shang's dog is a lucky one.</i>

33
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,840
<i>How could anything happen to him?</i>

34
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:55,240
<i>It's probably just inflamed.</i>

35
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,880
<i>Put some iodine on it</i>
<i>and keep an eye on it.</i>

36
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,040
<i>Don't worry.</i>

37
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,640
You'll be fine. Come on.
Let's put some medicine on your paw.

38
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,280
Let's go.

39
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,640
Over here.

40
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:15,560
THINKING OF YOU THIS SECOND
SEEING YOU THE NEXT

41
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,760
Sit. Come here.

42
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,840
Sit.

43
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,240
Sit.

44
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:32,880
Come on, let's put some medicine on it.

45
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:34,760
You can eat after we're done.

46
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,280
Give me your paw.

47
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:38,960
Come on.

48
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:41,360
Hold still.

49
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,600
Good. Almost done.

50
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,920
Let me see.

51
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,640
All done. Here.

52
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,080
Eat.

53
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:00,520
Sit.

54
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,520
Sit.

55
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,080
Eat.

56
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,760
ZANG YAO

57
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:11,040
<i>I'm leaving.</i>

58
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,400
<i>Want to meet?</i>

59
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:16,960
Sure.

60
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:31,400
The meat here really is different.

61
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,320
It smells amazing.

62
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,520
Need a hand?

63
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,480
No.

64
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:53,680
Your window is held together with tape?

65
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,760
It seals the gaps.

66
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,160
What made you suddenly decide
to come see me?

67
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,400
Wasn't I in Inner Mongolia
looking for investors?

68
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,440
I figured I wasn't that far from you.

69
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:07,920
Just a train ride away.

70
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,360
So I came to see you.

71
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:15,080
Twelve hours by train
isn't exactly nearby.

72
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,040
True enough.

73
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:21,160
It was so last minute.

74
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,280
The sleeper tickets were sold out.

75
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,720
I sat the whole way here.

76
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,120
My back is killing me.

77
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,120
Is there a hotel nearby?

78
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,080
I'll settle in for the night first.

79
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:37,120
The nearest guesthouse
is three hours away.

80
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,880
Three hours?

81
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,880
Then what do we do?

82
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,440
- You sleep here.
- I'll sleep over there.

83
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:51,160
- You take the bed.
- You…

84
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,680
I'll take the couch.

85
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,600
- I'll take the couch.
- I'll…

86
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:57,920
Let's eat first.

87
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,560
Okay.

88
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:05,000
Try this.

89
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,200
Sit.

90
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:27,280
Weren't you planning to stay
in Beijing for another two years?

91
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,240
Not anymore.

92
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:38,880
Whose dog is this?

93
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,120
Mine.

94
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:44,520
I've known you for years.

95
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,000
You'd never get a dog.

96
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,640
If you were going to get one,
it'd be a Tibetan Mastiff.

97
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:51,840
It's Shang Zhitao's dog, isn't it?

98
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,760
Yeah. It's her dog.

99
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
When are you leaving?

100
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,080
The day after tomorrow.

101
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:02,920
So soon?

102
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,240
Beijing isn't interesting anymore.

103
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,240
I'm going back to the UK.

104
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,480
At this point,

105
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:14,560
Beijing doesn't really have anything
to do with me anymore.

106
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,960
Have you made up your mind?

107
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:23,960
Whether I have or not,
would it change anything?

108
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:28,320
I came back for you.

109
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:31,360
But if you're no longer
the person you used to be,

110
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,280
how could I force you?

111
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,880
Or are you saying that to make me stay,

112
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,039
you'd give me what I've always wanted?

113
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,160
He's pretty loyal.

114
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,520
Keeping an eye on you for his owner.

115
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,840
Then I wish you a safe journey

116
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:55,000
and that everything
goes your way from now on.

117
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,720
Luan Nian.

118
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:04,040
Won't you give me one last hug?

119
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,720
All right.

120
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,120
Let's go.

121
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,320
Go.

122
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,040
Go.

123
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:48,600
Go.

124
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,760
Luan Nian.

125
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,280
Goodbye.

126
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,760
Keeping an eye on me for your owner, huh?

127
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,520
What are we now?

128
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,520
Why would you do that?

129
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,280
Let's go home.

130
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,880
Come on.

131
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,360
Yuanzhu.

132
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,440
Are you sleepy?

133
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,720
I'm a little scared.

134
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,520
I can't fall asleep.

135
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:55,520
I thought nothing ever scared you.

136
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,400
Listen.

137
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:01,320
Listen to the wind
rustling the window paper.

138
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,400
Then start counting.

139
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:06,920
One, two, three.

140
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,720
You'll be asleep before you know it.

141
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,480
Give it a try.

142
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,000
I still can't sleep.

143
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:31,800
How about you keep me company for a while?

144
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:34,760
Go ahead.

145
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:38,800
When you're away on business by yourself,

146
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,120
do you miss home?

147
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:47,760
Of course I do.

148
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:53,080
Your hometown is up
in the mountains, right?

149
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:57,360
After this business trip,
I'll go back with you and take a look.

150
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,480
I meant my home in Beijing.

151
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,680
Aren't you, Lei, and Tao my family?

152
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,040
Of course we are.

153
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,120
Yuanzhu.

154
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,280
Mr. Genius.

155
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:36,440
Do you think I'm a good person?

156
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,840
You are.

157
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:44,040
You're my best friend and family.

158
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,400
Look.

159
00:12:56,480 --> 00:13:02,440
We've been living under the same roof
for over three years.

160
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:05,800
I really like your cooking.

161
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:11,640
And I don't think you dislike me either.

162
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:16,080
Honestly…

163
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,520
When friends and family come to see me,
it makes me really happy.

164
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,880
Especially you. You're my best friend.

165
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:24,880
How about this?

166
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,560
Tomorrow afternoon I'll take you
for lamb with Mongolian chives.

167
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,000
It's our most authentic local specialty.

168
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,320
Then I'll take you to the station.

169
00:13:31,080 --> 00:13:33,200
Or I can book you a hotel
for tomorrow night.

170
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:34,640
You can stay
a couple more days if you want.

171
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,680
It's just that I have work
these next two days,

172
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,040
so I probably won't be able
to keep you company.

173
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:40,840
Don't be mad at me.

174
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:49,320
Don't say things like that.

175
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,600
It doesn't sound sincere.

176
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:56,800
If anyone should apologize,
it should be me.

177
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:59,880
Don't be upset that I suddenly showed up
and caused you trouble.

178
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:07,240
You don't need to worry about me tomorrow.

179
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:08,280
I'll just look around on my own.

180
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,880
And I'll…

181
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,360
I'll… I'll buy my own ticket back.

182
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:16,520
You don't have to worry about me.

183
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:17,920
I'll get the ticket.

184
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:20,920
It's late. Get some sleep.

185
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:22,920
You've had a long day.

186
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:25,000
I'm a little tired too.

187
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:30,720
Good night.

188
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:48,720
The wind really is strong.

189
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,080
Let's count.

190
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,480
Didn't you say

191
00:14:57,920 --> 00:14:59,640
counting helps you fall asleep?

192
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:02,400
One.

193
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,000
Two.

194
00:15:05,960 --> 00:15:06,840
Three.

195
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,680
Four.

196
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,400
Five.

197
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,280
Six.

198
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,320
Seven.

199
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,160
<i>How's Luke?</i>

200
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,600
<i>Is his paw still inflamed?</i>

201
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:35,800
Not good.

202
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:38,640
How could it not be?

203
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:41,040
<i>Let me see him.</i>

204
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:43,160
Here.

205
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,160
<i>See? He's perfectly fine. You're lying.</i>

206
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:50,600
<i>Luke.</i>

207
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,720
That silly dog does nothing but bark.

208
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:54,640
He's so noisy.

209
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:59,240
Well, how are you?

210
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:02,760
Still alive. Getting by.

211
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,480
How about you?

212
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,240
You are calling this late.

213
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,520
Are you working overtime?

214
00:16:10,840 --> 00:16:12,280
How's the work environment in Hangzhou?

215
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,000
Getting used to the new team?

216
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,240
Do you want the truth or a lie?

217
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,000
The truth.

218
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:27,840
I think Dony
is a very clear-headed leader.

219
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:30,440
The instructions he gives everyone
are always very clear.

220
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,120
You'll be sold down the river
and still thank them for it.

221
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:39,640
Look at you. You asked for the truth.

222
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:42,280
I'm just trying to know my opponent
before the battle.

223
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,000
What battle?

224
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:45,920
He's your boss.

225
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:49,720
You seem pretty hostile toward him.

226
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,080
<i>Do you two have history?</i>

227
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:54,480
<i>No.</i>

228
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,480
From now on, when you call,

229
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:57,400
don't sound like
you're reporting to your boss.

230
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:01,080
Just tell me when you're coming back.

231
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:02,640
I'll be waiting for you.

232
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,200
I'll come back as soon as I'm done.

233
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:44,640
<i>I just meant that in the workplace,</i>
<i>no one's doing anyone a favor.</i>

234
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:46,320
<i>There's no need to act</i>
<i>like you're above everyone else.</i>

235
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:50,640
Don't catch a cold.

236
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,720
You should head back.

237
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:56,240
<i>These are your New Year's gifts.</i>

238
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,440
<i>How about I treat you?</i>

239
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,920
<i>Let's go see a movie tonight.</i>

240
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,560
<i>You said it.</i>

241
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,560
<i>It wasn't easy for the four of us</i>
<i>to become friends.</i>

242
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,960
<i>We'll always look out for you.</i>

243
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,840
<i>Every gathering must come to an end.</i>

244
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:12,920
<i>People come and go.</i>

245
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,280
<i>That's just part of life.</i>

246
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:57,200
What do you think of Dony's abilities?

247
00:18:57,280 --> 00:18:58,000
DONY'S CV

248
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:00,480
I've heard he's pretty capable.

249
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:05,080
He's very clear-headed
and has a clear strategy for the division.

250
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:08,400
Are you complimenting him?

251
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,360
At the meeting last time,

252
00:19:11,440 --> 00:19:13,480
I thought you were pretty hard on him.

253
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,600
Did you know each other before?

254
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,040
Yes, but I'd rather never meet him again.

255
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,880
You don't think he came
to Lime because of you, do you?

256
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,840
Let's hope not.

257
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:29,360
I've worked in HR
at Lime for so many years.

258
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,720
He's the first person
who didn't go through

259
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:32,720
our HR department
before being assigned here.

260
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:36,000
And as soon as he arrived,
he took over your New Media team.

261
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:39,760
I don't think it's that simple.

262
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,240
Did you do a background check on him?

263
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,840
He was hired directly by the board.

264
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:48,360
How was our department
supposed to do a background check?

265
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,840
Then I suggest you do it.

266
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,800
You might find a surprise.

267
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,200
Don't worry.

268
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,560
I'm already looking into it.

269
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,360
Come eat.

270
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:20,920
Here.

271
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,640
The meat pie's hot. Eat slowly.

272
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,360
Don't burn your mouth.

273
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,040
Slow down. I'm not
going to take it from you.

274
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,680
Have some vegetables.

275
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:39,960
Silly dog.

276
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:50,920
Hello?

277
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:53,560
Your silly dog is eating the meat pie.

278
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,000
Have you eaten?

279
00:20:55,520 --> 00:20:56,720
<i>What are you having for dinner?</i>

280
00:20:58,120 --> 00:20:59,360
I'm going to stir-fry a couple of dishes.

281
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,920
<i>And make some osmanthus milk.</i>

282
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:03,760
Why?

283
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,520
You want some?

284
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:10,400
Then come back soon if you do.

285
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:12,720
<i>You'll have to wait for me.</i>

286
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,040
Why are you back?

287
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,720
I came back to report something for work,
then I'm leaving.

288
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:03,320
I missed you.

289
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:28,840
Everyone,

290
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:33,200
to more efficiently advance
the New Media campaign

291
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,600
for Xizi Cultural Tourism Group,

292
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:37,160
the company has decided
to form a dedicated project team

293
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,600
to be stationed on-site
for in-depth operations.

294
00:22:41,120 --> 00:22:42,240
The team members are as follows.

295
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,360
Kitty.

296
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:46,080
Claire. Leo.

297
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,720
Kangkang. Sunny.

298
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:49,400
Kami. William.

299
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:51,200
Lucy. Flora.

300
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,400
Dony.

301
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:59,760
I've always been responsible
for the Beijing New Media team.

302
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:01,120
I won't be going this time.

303
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:02,840
I'll stay in Beijing
and support all of you.

304
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:05,520
Anyone can opt out, except you.

305
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:09,280
You'll be leading
this dedicated project team.

306
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,520
Let's wrap up the meeting here.

307
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:22,000
Flora.

308
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,240
Come have a seat.

309
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:35,760
I've read your report on this project.

310
00:23:35,840 --> 00:23:37,120
You did an excellent job.

311
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,040
You identified the key issues
very accurately.

312
00:23:39,960 --> 00:23:42,920
And the three core client concerns
you raised

313
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:46,200
are exactly what we need
to address first at the workshop.

314
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:48,120
Well done.

315
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:49,520
Thank you, Dony.

316
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:56,960
Do you trust Luke?

317
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:05,120
Luke is very capable,
and he's strict with all of us.

318
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:07,600
We've learned a lot from him.

319
00:24:07,680 --> 00:24:09,240
We all respect him.

320
00:24:11,160 --> 00:24:13,320
Flora, you need to understand this.

321
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:17,120
Anyone in that position,
with the resources it comes with,

322
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,200
would appear highly capable.

323
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:22,200
Anyone in that position
would have that halo.

324
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:24,640
Don't be blinded by it.

325
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:28,000
I looked into your background.

326
00:24:28,080 --> 00:24:29,440
You earned your place
in the New Media Division

327
00:24:29,520 --> 00:24:30,600
through open competition.

328
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:33,920
This project is another opportunity.

329
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:36,640
You can learn just as much
by working with me,

330
00:24:36,720 --> 00:24:39,200
and you'll be promoted much faster.

331
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:52,200
Dony is clearly trying to poach people
and expand his team.

332
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:54,320
Are you sure you want to take leave
at a time like this?

333
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,120
So you're saying
I should fight for it too?

334
00:24:57,720 --> 00:24:59,640
Have two opposing pawns
fight tooth and nail,

335
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:04,120
so the board can sit back
and enjoy the show?

336
00:25:06,320 --> 00:25:08,760
I guess you're retreating to advance.

337
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:13,200
But you've retreated too far,
letting your opponent seize the advantage.

338
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:16,560
It won't be easy
to turn things around after that.

339
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:21,720
Senior,

340
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:24,560
thank you for putting up with me
all these years.

341
00:25:25,120 --> 00:25:27,480
And no matter what,
you've always been on my side.

342
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:31,160
But I'd also ask you
to keep an eye on the new guy.

343
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:33,760
If he really goes too far,

344
00:25:33,840 --> 00:25:36,720
we'll be the ones
left to clean up the mess.

345
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:39,200
Exactly.

346
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:40,760
That's what I'm worried about.

347
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Today the board can bypass us
and bring in Dony.

348
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:47,160
Tomorrow they could easily
send us an HRBP.

349
00:25:48,200 --> 00:25:50,040
Hurry up and process my annual leave.

350
00:25:50,560 --> 00:25:51,640
I'm taking some time off to clear my head.

351
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:54,040
If I'm in a good mood,

352
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,800
I might even help you prepare
for what's coming.

353
00:25:57,600 --> 00:25:58,720
Thanks, Junior.

354
00:25:58,800 --> 00:25:59,920
You're welcome.

355
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,320
Thank you, my dear Senior.

356
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,080
Dony's a really nice guy.

357
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:17,880
He doesn't put on airs at all.

358
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,400
Yesterday, he even asked me

359
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:22,040
if work was going smoothly
and whether I lived far away.

360
00:26:22,840 --> 00:26:24,360
He really is easy to get along with.

361
00:26:24,440 --> 00:26:25,480
He asked me yesterday too.

362
00:26:25,560 --> 00:26:27,560
He wanted to know what I like to do

363
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:29,520
and what I usually do on weekends.

364
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:31,000
He even asked if I had a boyfriend.

365
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:34,280
He said there are a lot of outstanding
young men at headquarters

366
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:35,680
and that I should get
to know some of them.

367
00:26:38,080 --> 00:26:39,120
Tao.

368
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:48,240
Dony's way of winning people over
is really straightforward.

369
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,880
I heard the board
sent him to replace Luke.

370
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:54,840
The board isn't happy with Luke.

371
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:55,760
They think he's too hard to manage.

372
00:27:18,240 --> 00:27:20,520
Where did this young golden boy come from?

373
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:24,840
Excuse me. Who's Lumi?

374
00:27:27,440 --> 00:27:28,280
I am.

375
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:31,640
And you are?

376
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,440
What's going on?

377
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:55,720
I don't know
where HR found this old academic.

378
00:27:56,320 --> 00:27:58,880
What kind of so-called
marketing expert is he?

379
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,920
Why do I have to report everything to him?

380
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,240
Even Luan Nian couldn't control me.

381
00:28:02,320 --> 00:28:05,720
Now he's setting all these rules
for me to follow.

382
00:28:05,800 --> 00:28:07,000
Why should I?

383
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:09,360
What's going on?

384
00:28:11,640 --> 00:28:13,120
Luke just went on leave,

385
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:15,600
and the company brings in
this marketing expert.

386
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,080
This Will…

387
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:22,440
Could Dony have sent him
to make things difficult for me?

388
00:28:23,560 --> 00:28:24,400
No, wait.

389
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:27,280
Dony can even interfere
with HR's responsibilities now?

390
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:29,960
On this business trip,

391
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:32,200
you have to keep a close eye
on things for Luan Nian.

392
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:35,320
Don't worry.

393
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:39,760
No.

394
00:28:40,280 --> 00:28:41,160
I can't just sit back and do nothing.

395
00:28:41,840 --> 00:28:44,520
I have to find out
where this old academic came from.

396
00:28:58,880 --> 00:29:01,440
HANGZHOU

397
00:29:01,520 --> 00:29:02,440
- <i>Dony.</i>
- <i>You're here.</i>

398
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:05,160
Have a seat.

399
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,680
Flora. Don't sit by the door.

400
00:29:09,760 --> 00:29:11,080
Sit over here.

401
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,400
Dony.

402
00:29:23,480 --> 00:29:25,800
This fish
is this restaurant's signature dish.

403
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:27,120
Please, try some.

404
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:31,960
You first.

405
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:33,480
Thank you.

406
00:29:35,360 --> 00:29:39,360
I think the key visual
for this project is extremely creative.

407
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:40,960
Kangkang did a great job.

408
00:29:41,720 --> 00:29:43,080
Thank you, Dony. Just doing my job.

409
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:44,960
No need to be so polite.

410
00:29:45,680 --> 00:29:48,400
Now that our dedicated project team
has been formed, we're one family.

411
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:49,920
We're one team.

412
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:50,880
Just call me Dony.

413
00:29:50,960 --> 00:29:52,720
Treat this like you're at home.

414
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:55,960
Relax, everyone. Don't hold back.

415
00:29:56,040 --> 00:29:57,080
Come on. Cheers.

416
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:00,960
I… I can't drink.
I'll toast with water instead.

417
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:04,080
I don't drink much either.
I'll use tea instead.

418
00:30:05,160 --> 00:30:07,320
It's just wine. One glass won't hurt.

419
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:09,000
It's even good for your skin.

420
00:30:09,080 --> 00:30:10,200
Just one glass.

421
00:30:10,800 --> 00:30:11,800
Here.

422
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:29,760
This toast is to wish
our dedicated project team

423
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:32,840
great success here in Hangzhou.

424
00:30:32,920 --> 00:30:33,800
Cheers.

425
00:30:35,920 --> 00:30:36,960
To a great success.

426
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:40,200
Kangkang, it's okay.

427
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:41,480
If you don't want to drink, don't.

428
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:43,400
At Lime, we have a tradition.

429
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:44,720
We drink, but we never pressure anyone to.

430
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:47,000
Especially not our female employees.

431
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:52,760
Dony, you were just excited, right?

432
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:54,520
He was only asking us to take a sip.

433
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:58,120
Flora's right.

434
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:02,280
Just a sip is enough. Don't drink anymore.

435
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,680
Flora. Do you have a boyfriend?

436
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:15,120
That's a private matter,
so I'd rather not say.

437
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:17,320
Why keep it a secret?

438
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:20,480
I don't mind saying it. I'm single.

439
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:25,880
Dony,

440
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:28,840
this toast is for you.

441
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:31,920
Thank you for bringing us here to learn.

442
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:34,600
Take your time. I'll finish mine.

443
00:31:45,520 --> 00:31:46,720
Look at Kitty.

444
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:51,120
That's what I call bringing energy to work
and passion to life.

445
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:53,480
Everyone should learn from her.

446
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:55,160
Come on.

447
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:03,480
I need to take this. Excuse me.

448
00:32:13,600 --> 00:32:15,000
A stroke?

449
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:17,120
When did it happen?

450
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:18,760
Is it serious?

451
00:32:19,600 --> 00:32:20,640
They caught it in time.

452
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:21,720
He's not in any danger.

453
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:25,920
I'm calling because

454
00:32:26,000 --> 00:32:28,040
I've got an urgent job
that has to be submitted today.

455
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:29,560
You worked on this project before,

456
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:32,360
so I was hoping you could help me.

457
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,320
Don't worry.

458
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:35,560
I'll take care of all the work for you.

459
00:32:36,160 --> 00:32:38,400
<i>Can you handle everything</i>
<i>at the hospital by yourself?</i>

460
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:39,480
I think so.

461
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:41,640
My mom and I are taking shifts,
and we'll hire a caregiver.

462
00:32:42,240 --> 00:32:44,560
<i>I'll be at the hospital</i>
<i>the next couple of days.</i>

463
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:48,360
I'm just worried
that jerk Will won't approve my leave.

464
00:32:49,320 --> 00:32:52,080
He can't be that unreasonable.

465
00:32:52,160 --> 00:32:53,480
<i>You never know.</i>

466
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:56,040
He just chewed me out
at yesterday's meeting.

467
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:59,480
<i>For clocking in and out on time</i>
<i>and being irresponsible.</i>

468
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,640
<i>What an old fossil.</i>

469
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:03,200
What's wrong with clocking
in and out on time? What's wrong?

470
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,640
Exactly. He doesn't know
how good our Lumi is

471
00:33:05,720 --> 00:33:07,760
at managing her time.

472
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:11,600
Now I'm completely convinced
he's Dony's plant.

473
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:13,880
<i>They're trying to drive away</i>
<i>that stubborn mule's right-hand men,</i>

474
00:33:13,960 --> 00:33:15,360
<i>and once they do, they've won.</i>

475
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:19,440
How are things on Dony's side?

476
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:20,800
Busy?

477
00:33:23,040 --> 00:33:24,440
Not at all. Everything's going well.

478
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:27,520
<i>If you need anything, just let me know.</i>

479
00:33:27,600 --> 00:33:29,160
I'll handle it for you remotely.

480
00:33:30,360 --> 00:33:32,200
It won't affect work at all. Don't worry.

481
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:34,720
Okay.

482
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:35,880
Then I'll take you up on that.

483
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:37,560
<i>I'll go ask for leave.</i>

484
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:43,080
I'm sure that old fossil
is only going to ask one thing.

485
00:33:43,960 --> 00:33:44,800
The reason?

486
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:47,360
My father was hospitalized after a stroke.

487
00:33:50,840 --> 00:33:52,080
Submit your leave request
through the proper process.

488
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,440
Make sure your work
is properly handed over.

489
00:33:57,320 --> 00:33:58,520
That's it?

490
00:34:00,960 --> 00:34:02,080
What else?

491
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:08,000
Thanks.

492
00:34:09,600 --> 00:34:10,719
Close the door.

493
00:35:31,840 --> 00:35:33,840
‪I feel there’s still a bit of an issue.

494
00:35:33,920 --> 00:35:35,960
Check this line.

495
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,360
I think there's a problem.

496
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:38,640
I'll check it.

497
00:35:39,320 --> 00:35:40,360
Just leave it here.

498
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:41,360
Flora.

499
00:35:46,080 --> 00:35:47,120
Kitty.

500
00:35:53,480 --> 00:35:54,320
Flora.

501
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:58,240
Why does this budget
have to be approved by Luke?

502
00:35:59,640 --> 00:36:02,160
Lime's budget management
has three core components.

503
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:04,680
They include the approval process
and time limits.

504
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:06,520
They're all clearly defined.

505
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,800
Dony, you should know that, shouldn't you?

506
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:11,600
All right.

507
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,840
I'll follow the budget approval process.

508
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,000
I'll get going.

509
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,680
None of the top MCN resources
from our Beijing office can be used.

510
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:33,840
Everything has to go through
the Hangzhou headquarters now.

511
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:35,680
Isn't that basically
starting from scratch?

512
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:39,720
The client just asked me
why this New Media campaign

513
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:41,720
was suddenly moved
from Beijing to Hangzhou.

514
00:36:42,680 --> 00:36:44,320
They think the Beijing team
is more experienced

515
00:36:44,400 --> 00:36:45,520
and has better resources.

516
00:36:45,600 --> 00:36:46,480
They're concerned about the results.

517
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,880
I didn't even know how to explain it.

518
00:36:50,480 --> 00:36:54,000
Just tell them
Hangzhou is an emerging city

519
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:57,000
with enormous potential
that's poised for rapid growth.

520
00:36:57,080 --> 00:36:58,400
Potential?

521
00:36:58,480 --> 00:36:59,720
Based on the data,

522
00:36:59,800 --> 00:37:02,160
how does Hangzhou's new media ecosystem
or top-tier resources

523
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:03,840
compare to Beijing's?

524
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:05,960
The resources aren't there.

525
00:37:06,040 --> 00:37:07,200
The client's concerned.

526
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:08,680
And the team's working themselves
to the bone.

527
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:11,320
Where's Dony?

528
00:37:12,280 --> 00:37:14,160
I heard he's out
doing market research again.

529
00:37:14,840 --> 00:37:15,920
I saw Dony

530
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,960
downstairs this morning
carrying a pot of orchids.

531
00:37:18,040 --> 00:37:19,320
They were beautiful.

532
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:21,280
You could tell they were expensive.

533
00:37:21,360 --> 00:37:23,320
Yeah. Yesterday it was an art gallery.

534
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:24,960
The day before, a tea house.

535
00:37:25,040 --> 00:37:26,120
So what came of all that research?

536
00:37:26,200 --> 00:37:27,840
How are we supposed
to explain it to the client?

537
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:31,080
Tell them our boss went off
to drink tea and admire flowers?

538
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:32,560
Let's just focus on our own work for now.

539
00:37:32,640 --> 00:37:33,960
When Dony gets back,

540
00:37:34,040 --> 00:37:36,240
ask him to give us clearer instructions
as soon as possible.

541
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:49,400
BUDGET REQUEST APPROVED

542
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:52,840
<i>Why does this budget</i>
<i>have to be approved by Luke?</i>

543
00:37:58,600 --> 00:37:59,760
Hello?

544
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:02,160
- Did I interrupt you?
- <i>No.</i>

545
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:04,480
I was walking Luke.

546
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:05,680
What's up?

547
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:11,200
Did you receive
the two budget requests from Dony?

548
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:12,160
No.

549
00:38:13,200 --> 00:38:15,360
Is Dony in a rush
and asked you to follow up with me?

550
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:16,560
No.

551
00:38:16,640 --> 00:38:17,960
According to the process,

552
00:38:18,040 --> 00:38:19,920
those two budget requests need your
signature before they can take effect.

553
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:21,400
But somehow they skipped you.

554
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:24,400
<i>I've already received</i>
<i>the payment notification.</i>

555
00:38:26,160 --> 00:38:28,160
I don't think the system
would miss something like that.

556
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:31,040
Got it.

557
00:38:31,960 --> 00:38:33,600
Has he given you
a hard time anywhere else?

558
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:35,240
No.

559
00:38:35,320 --> 00:38:37,120
He's hardly ever in the office.

560
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:41,880
By the way, give me Sun Yu's number.

561
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:43,920
A friend of mine in investment banking
wants to meet her.

562
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,160
<i>Maybe they'll invest in her.</i>

563
00:38:50,680 --> 00:38:51,600
Thank you.

564
00:38:52,440 --> 00:38:53,560
I mean it.

565
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:57,120
All right, then.

566
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:01,920
Let's go. Luke.

567
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:21,280
Coming.

568
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:29,480
- Kitty.
- Flora.

569
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:31,960
Sorry to bother you so late.

570
00:39:32,520 --> 00:39:33,600
Could you do me a favor?

571
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:35,640
Sure.

572
00:39:40,240 --> 00:39:43,440
Could you report to Dony for me?

573
00:39:45,120 --> 00:39:46,360
Me?

574
00:39:46,960 --> 00:39:47,920
Yes.

575
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:51,200
I… I still have some backend data
to finish processing.

576
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:52,480
I'm a little pressed for time.

577
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:55,160
But I've already finished the proposal.

578
00:39:57,280 --> 00:39:58,320
No problem. I'll go.

579
00:40:00,320 --> 00:40:01,520
Great. Thanks.

580
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:03,080
No problem.

581
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,560
Flora.

582
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:11,120
If anything comes up later,
call me anytime.

583
00:40:11,200 --> 00:40:13,920
I'll be around. I can come over.

584
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:17,160
Don't you need
to finish processing the data?

585
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:23,520
Yeah. But Dony
can be pretty particular about work.

586
00:40:23,600 --> 00:40:25,680
When you report to him,

587
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:27,400
pay attention to how you approach it.

588
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:31,440
Don't worry.

589
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:35,680
Okay.

590
00:40:55,520 --> 00:40:56,520
Why haven't you left yet?

591
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:01,120
Let's go together.

592
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,040
Flora.

593
00:41:12,560 --> 00:41:13,600
Kitty.

594
00:41:16,960 --> 00:41:17,840
Kitty.

595
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:31,560
Are you afraid of Dony?

596
00:41:36,280 --> 00:41:37,480
<i>The background check results are in.</i>

597
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:40,640
During his time at his previous company,

598
00:41:40,720 --> 00:41:42,600
Dony came under strong suspicion
of embezzlement.

599
00:41:44,240 --> 00:41:46,080
And it involved
a substantial amount of money.

600
00:41:49,560 --> 00:41:50,400
Specifically?

601
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:54,120
He skimmed money through price differences
in supplier contracts.

602
00:41:54,200 --> 00:41:55,880
It wasn't a particularly
sophisticated scheme,

603
00:41:55,960 --> 00:41:58,800
but the investigation was quietly dropped.

604
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:01,840
He left the company on the grounds
of personal career development.

605
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:04,400
That does fit his usual style.

606
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:06,600
I don't get it.

607
00:42:06,680 --> 00:42:09,120
How could someone with such
a serious black mark on his record

608
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:13,640
be parachuted in by the board
to keep you in check?

609
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:17,320
Who was it on the board
that brought Dony in?

610
00:42:18,600 --> 00:42:20,120
Mr. He. He Qiming.

611
00:42:22,000 --> 00:42:25,040
Last year, He Qiming strongly backed
that Southeast Asia project.

612
00:42:25,120 --> 00:42:27,000
I joined forces with several shareholders
to vote it down.

613
00:42:27,600 --> 00:42:29,080
I guess he felt humiliated.

614
00:42:29,640 --> 00:42:31,440
Divide and balance power. Create chaos.

615
00:42:32,560 --> 00:42:34,560
He just wants to see me fail.

616
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:35,680
It's obvious.

617
00:42:36,600 --> 00:42:40,120
So, Dony works for him?

618
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:42,200
More like a puppet.

619
00:42:42,840 --> 00:42:46,520
A puppet who's willing
to go head-to-head with me.

620
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:11,480
Dony, we're here
to give you a work update.

621
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:17,680
Could he be laundering money for Mr. He?

622
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:19,600
Send Lumi to Hangzhou.

623
00:43:20,240 --> 00:43:22,240
Follow the trail back to the source.

624
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:23,960
No.

625
00:43:24,040 --> 00:43:26,280
Lumi is known to be your right hand.

626
00:43:26,360 --> 00:43:28,440
If you do that, won't you tip them off?

627
00:43:29,520 --> 00:43:30,600
That's exactly the point.

628
00:43:31,480 --> 00:43:35,640
I want Lumi to openly investigate
the cash flow, ownership structure,

629
00:43:35,720 --> 00:43:38,160
and beneficial owners
behind those companies.

630
00:43:38,240 --> 00:43:39,680
Peel back the layers,

631
00:43:39,760 --> 00:43:41,280
and eventually we'll expose
the person behind it all.

632
00:43:43,960 --> 00:43:45,080
You're good at this.

633
00:44:19,600 --> 00:44:20,800
You're still up?

634
00:44:23,600 --> 00:44:27,200
Sun Yu's project
isn't performing very well.

635
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:28,880
I'm helping her revise her business plan.

636
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:38,840
Sun Yu's making a dating app?

637
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:42,720
Take a look at this proposal for me.

638
00:44:42,800 --> 00:44:44,520
You're the expert
when it comes to investments.

639
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:58,000
The business plan isn't strong enough.

640
00:44:58,080 --> 00:44:59,040
The data isn't convincing enough.

641
00:44:59,800 --> 00:45:01,040
And the key selling points
don't stand out.

642
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,280
Then,

643
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:08,640
how can a proposal attract investors?

644
00:45:09,240 --> 00:45:12,200
Shang Zhitao, I'm on leave,
and you're still making me work.

645
00:45:23,200 --> 00:45:24,880
It's not like
you've got anything else to do.

646
00:45:25,680 --> 00:45:27,240
Help me polish the business plan.

647
00:45:34,680 --> 00:45:35,960
Now you're pushing your luck.
